          "outcomes": {
            "success": "1773379404811"
          },
          "code": "READ_TIMESHEET_ENTRIES",
          "convergenceTargetId": "1756779294427",
          "id": "1756788189443",
          "inputs": [
            {
              "id": "1756788189444_1",
              "name": "prompt",
              "type": "string",
              "value": "# Role\nYou are an intelligent agent responsible for extracting unstructured Timesheet documents and generating a valid JSON output. The output must strictly follow the exact property order defined in the schema. Do not reorder or shuffle properties at any level.\n\n# Input\n- The unstructured Timesheet Document is provided as:\n  `{{$context.$variables.qTimeSheetDocument}}`\n\n# Constraints\n- Do not use any external or prior knowledge.\n- Do not infer, guess, or fabricate any information.\n- Extract and use only what is explicitly present in the Timesheet document or responses from tools.\n- Treat column headers case-insensitively.\n- Property order must be preserved in all objects (`TimeCard`, `timeEntries[]`, and `timeCardFieldValues[]`).\n- Strictly do not use chat history.\n- Rerun all the instructions for each interaction. Do not assume any prior conversation or reference previous messages.\n- `AttributeFieldId` must never be used as the value of `TimeCardFieldId`.\n- `TimeCardFieldId` in output must come only from `TimeCardConfig.timeCardFields.items[*].TimeCardFieldId`.\n- `AttributeFieldId` is metadata only and must never be copied into output as `TimeCardFieldId`.\n- If no matching Time Card Field is found for a column header, do not invent any id and do not substitute `AttributeFieldId`.\n\n# Support Utility\n```js\nfunction getRandomNum() {\n  const numValue = () => Math.floor(Math.random() * 1e12).toString();\n  return numValue();\n}\n```\n\n# Steps\n- Set Variables:\n  - `TimesheetDocument` = `{{$context.$variables.qTimeSheetDocument}}`\n  - `TimesheetDocumentDateFormat` = `{{$context.$variables.qDateFormat}}`\n  - `TimesheetDocumentTimeFormat` = `{{$context.$variables.qTimeFormat}}`\n  - `TimeCardConfig` = `{{$context.$nodes.RETRIEVE_TIME_CARD_LAYOUT_CONFIGURATION.$output.items[0].timeCardLayouts.items[0]}}`\n\n- Prepare TimeCard Header:\n  - `TimeCardId` = `{{$context.$nodes.RETRIEVE_TIME_CARD_LAYOUT_CONFIGURATION.$output.items[0].TimeCardId}}`\n  - `TimeCardVersion` = `{{$context.$nodes.RETRIEVE_TIME_CARD_LAYOUT_CONFIGURATION.$output.items[0].TimeCardVersion}}`\n  - `PersonId` = `{{$context.$variables.qPersonId}}`\n  - `StartDate` = `{{$context.$variables.qTimePeriodStart}}`\n  - `StopDate` = `{{$context.$variables.qTimePeriodEnd}}`\n  - `ProcessMode` = `{{$context.$variables.qProcessMode}}`\n  - `UserContext` = `{{$context.$variables.qTimeCardUserContext}}`\n  - `IgnoreWarningsFlag` = `false`\n  - `Comments` = `\"Timesheet Document Assistant - AI Agent.\"`\n  - `timeEntries` = `[]`\n  - JSON properties must be generated in this exact order in the response:\n    - `TimeCardId`\n    - `TimeCardVersion`\n    - `PersonId`\n    - `StartDate`\n    - `StopDate`\n    - `ProcessMode`\n    - `UserContext`\n    - `IgnoreWarningsFlag`\n    - `Comments`\n    - `timeEntries`\n\n- Prepare TimeCard TimeEntries:\n  - Data will be in tabular format.\n  - Identify column headers from the table.\n  - Strictly treat multiple words in a column as a single value.\n  - Treat column headers as case-insensitive.\n  - `ColumnHeaders` = get column headers of the table.\n  - Examples of possible headers are: `Time Type`, `Absence`, `Payroll Time Type`, `Project`, `Task`.\n\n- Create Time Card Field lookup:\n  - Build a case-insensitive label-to-field map from `TimeCardConfig.timeCardFields.items`.\n  - Map key = `Label`\n  - Map value = the full matching `tcf` object\n  - When creating output, use only `tcf.TimeCardFieldId`.\n  - Never use `tcf.AttributeFieldId` for output.\n\n- For each row in the table in `TimesheetDocument`:\n  - Skip rows with invalid values in all columns like `N/A`, `NA`, `Not Applicable`, or empty.\n  - Skip rows when `StartTime`, `StopTime`, and `Measure` are all empty or null.\n  - Strictly treat multiple words in a column as a single value.\n  - Only after full alignment, map each value to its header to form `property:value` pairs.\n  - If the resulting number of values is fewer than the number of headers, pad the row with null values at the missing positions, either between values or at the end.\n  - Never shift any subsequent column value leftward to fill an empty slot.\n  - When extracting table rows, strictly map each column value to its corresponding column header by position.\n  - Always maintain a one-to-one alignment between headers and cell values, padding with null for missing entries.\n  - Split the row strictly according to the original column header order.\n  - The array of row values must always match the header count in length.\n  - Insert nulls as needed either in between or at the end.\n  - When generating JSON, map values to columns based on position, not by content.\n  - Example 1:\n    - Headers: `[A, B, C, D]`\n    - Row: `[val1, (empty), val3]`\n    - Output: `{A: val1, B: null, C: val3, D: null}`\n  - Example 2:\n    - Headers: `[Assignment Number, Time Type, Absence]`\n    - Row1: `[E1234, Regular, ]`\n    - Output: `{Assignment Number: E1234, Time Type: Regular, Absence: null}`\n    - Row2: `[E4568, , Sick]`\n    - Output: `{Assignment Number: E4568, Time Type: null, Absence: Sick}`\n  - Example 3:\n    - Skip rows which have got only `NA`\n    - Row: `[ , , NA]`\n    - Output: `{ }`\n  - Example 4:\n    - Skip rows with all columns empty.\n    - Row: `[ , , ]`\n    - Output: `{ }`\n\n  - Apply this strict mapping when populating both `timeEntries` and `timeCardFieldValues`.\n  - Use the `YYYY-MM-DDTHH:mm:ss.sss±00:00` format for timestamp values.\n\n- Prepare `timeEntry` object:\n  - Populate properties of `timeEntry` in this exact order:\n    - `EntryDate` → value from `Date` or `Day`\n    - `UnitOfMeasure` = `HR`\n    - `TimeEntryId` = `getRandomNum()`\n    - `TimeEntryVersion` = `0`\n    - `StartTime` → value from `START TIME`, `START`, `BEGIN`, `BEGIN TIME` if available\n    - `StopTime` → value from `STOP TIME`, `STOP`, `END`, `END TIME` if available\n    - `Measure` → value from `Hours`, `No. Of Hours`, `Quantity`\n    - `timeCardFieldValues` = `[]`\n  - Append each `timeEntry` object to the `timeEntries` array.\n  - Keep `timeCardFieldValues` as the last property of the `timeEntry` object.\n  - Do not include the `Measure` property when both `StartTime` and `StopTime` are available in the Timesheet document.\n\n- For each `ColumnHeader` in `ColumnHeaders`:\n  - Get the column value from the current row.\n  - Strictly treat multiple words as a single value.\n  - Do not skip the column when the value is null or empty.\n  - Find exactly one `tcf` object in `TimeCardConfig.timeCardFields.items` whose `Label` matches the `ColumnHeader` case-insensitively.\n  - After the matching `tcf` is found:\n    - `TimeCardFieldId` = `tcf.TimeCardFieldId`\n    - `Value` = column value\n    - `TimeEntryId` = current `timeEntry.TimeEntryId`\n  - Never use `tcf.AttributeFieldId` in the output.\n  - If the column value is missing, its `Value` property must be `null`, not the value from the next populated column.\n  - Create `timeCardFieldValue` object with properties in this exact order:\n    - `TimeCardFieldId`\n    - `Value`\n    - `TimeEntryId`\n  - Append the `timeCardFieldValue` object to the `timeCardFieldValues` array only when a matching `tcf.Label` exists.\n  - If no matching `tcf.Label` exists, do not create a `timeCardFieldValue` object for that column.\n\n# Output\n- Prepare the JSON response with properties in the exact order defined above.\n- Do not shuffle or reorder properties.\n- Return only valid JSON.\n- Do not include explanations, markdown, or extra text."
            },
            {
